notes.body:
Latest update was not only for rebase but also for a slight improvement targetted at sub-dissectors.

Before the change, we had roughly this sequence in `dissect_thrift_common()` in case of T_REPLY:
```c
res = dissector_try_string(…, thrift_opt);
if (res > 0) {
    return data_offset + res;
}
subtree = proto_tree_add_subtree(…, &data_pi, "Data");
thrift_header_t header = dissect_thrift_field_header(…); // Take a peek at the first field header
if (header.field_id != 0) {
    // This T_REPLY is in fact an exception and /not/ the nominal return type
    proto_item_set_text(data_pi, "Exception: %d", header.field_id);
}
```
What changed is the additional reply_field_id which is filled before the sub-dissector is called:
```c
// Move the peek at the top.
thrift_header_t header = dissect_thrift_field_header(…); // Take a peek at the first field header
thrift_opt->reply_field_id = header.field_id; // Give the information to the sub-dissector.
// Now we continue as before.
res = dissector_try_string(…, thrift_opt);
if (res > 0) {
    return data_offset + res;
}
subtree = proto_tree_add_subtree(…, &data_pi, "Data");
// No need to re-read the header, we already have the value.
if (thrift_opt->reply_field_id != 0) {
    // This T_REPLY is in fact an exception and /not/ the nominal return type
    proto_item_set_text(data_pi, "Exception: %d", header.field_id);
}
```

This way sub-dissector directly know if the REPLY gives the normal result or an exception and for the later case, which exception.

I found this while preparing the documentation because my initial (proprietary) sub-dissector was manually getting this information in a non-agnostic way regarding binary or compact protocol. This change allows for a nice simplification on sub-dissector side.

